			"type": "yaml",
			"value": "title: Incremental Static Regeneration with Cache Components\ndescription: Learn how to prerender a subset of dynamic routes, serve App Shells for the rest, and upgrade them after the first visit.\nnav_title: ISR with Cache Components"
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../04-glossary.md#incremental-static-regeneration-isr",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR)"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " with "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../03-api-reference/05-config/01-next-config-js/cacheComponents.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "cacheComponents"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " and "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../03-api-reference/05-config/01-next-config-js/partialPrefetching.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Partial Prefetching"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " gives every route an instant first visit, even for URLs that weren't included in the build."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "During build, Partial Prerendering splits each render into two parts:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "list",
			"ordered": false,
			"start": null,
			"spread": false,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "The "
								},
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "App Shell"
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": ": the generic, reusable part of the page that doesn't depend on URL data"
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "The rest of the statically renderable content: the param-specific prerenders for the URLs you list in "
								},
								{
									"type": "link",
									"title": null,
									"url": "../03-api-reference/04-functions/generate-static-params.md",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "inlineCode",
											"value": "generateStaticParams"
										}
									]
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "For a visit to a URL whose params were included in "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "generateStaticParams"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", Next.js serves the fully prerendered page from the cache. For a visit to a URL whose params weren't, Next.js serves the App Shell instantly, then upgrades it in the background with the now-known params. Subsequent visits to that URL get the upgraded result from the cache, skipping the App Shell entirely."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "If you have used "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "./incremental-static-regeneration.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "ISR"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " or "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://nextjs.org/docs/pages/api-reference/functions/get-static-paths#fallback-true",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "fallback: true"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " in the Pages Router, this is the Cache Components equivalent."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Enable both "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../03-api-reference/05-config/01-next-config-js/cacheComponents.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "cacheComponents"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " and "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "../03-api-reference/05-config/01-next-config-js/partialPrefetching.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Partial Prefetching"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Cache Components prerenders a static shell that can include fallback UI. For paths not returned by "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "generateStaticParams"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ", Next.js can render the path on demand and store the completed result in the ISR cache."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Partial Prefetching determines whether the fallback is served before the URL-specific render completes:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "list",
			"ordered": false,
			"start": null,
			"spread": false,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "With Partial Prefetching:"
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " You can await "
								},
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "params"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " inside "
								},
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "<Suspense>"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": ". Next.js can immediately serve the fallback for an unlisted path, render the URL-specific content, and store the completed result in the ISR cache."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "Without Partial Prefetching:"
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " The first request for an unlisted path must wait for the URL-specific render to complete. Await "
								},
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "params"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " outside any "
								},
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "<Suspense>"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " boundary, including one created by "
								},
								{
									"type": "link",
									"title": null,
									"url": "../03-api-reference/03-file-conventions/loading.md",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "inlineCode",
											"value": "loading.tsx"
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": ", so Next.js creates an ISR entry for that URL."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "blockquote",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "paragraph",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "strong",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "Good to know:"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " Without Partial Prefetching, awaiting "
						},
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "params"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " inside "
						},
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "<Suspense>"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " causes Next.js to keep serving the shared fallback instead of creating a URL-specific ISR entry. Data fetched by the route can still be cached independently."
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "code",
			"lang": "ts",
			"meta": "filename=\"next.config.ts\" highlight={4-5}",
			"value": "import type { NextConfig } from 'next'\n\nconst nextConfig: NextConfig = {\n\tcacheComponents: true,\n\tpartialPrefetching: true,\n}\n\nexport default nextConfig"
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Example"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "We'll build a product catalog with category layouts and product detail pages using the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "https://next-recipe-api.vercel.dev/",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Recipe API"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": ". You can find the resources used in this example here:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "list",
			"ordered": false,
			"start": null,
			"spread": false,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
